pervision, or an unintentional failure to include something?","options":["supervision","unintentional omission","neither"],"answer":"unintentional omission","strata":{"frame":"anchored-noun","sense":"miss"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-02","english":"An unintentional omission in the packing list left the spare seal behind.","ainglish":"An overslip in the packing list left the spare seal behind.","question":"Does the sentence describe supervision or an accidental miss?","options":["neither","supervision","unintentional omission"],"answer":"unintentional omission","strata":{"frame":"cold-noun","sense":"miss"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-03","english":"The unintentional omission of the rollback flag caused the deployment to stall.","ainglish":"The overslip of the rollback flag caused the deployment to stall.","question":"What role does the named event play: monitoring the deployment, or accidentally leaving out the flag?","options":["unintentional omission","neither","supervision"],"answer":"unintentional omission","strata":{"frame":"genitive-noun","sense":"miss"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-04","english":"The checklist failure was an unintentional omission, not a deliberate exception.","ainglish":"The checklist failure was an overslip, not a deliberate exception.","question":"Was the checklist failure intentional, supervisory, or accidentally missed?","options":["supervision","unintentional omission","neither"],"answer":"unintentional omission","strata":{"frame":"contrast-noun","sense":"miss"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-05","english":"We unintentionally failed to notice the expired certificate before the restart.","ainglish":"We overslipped the expired certificate before the restart.","question":"Did the team accidentally miss the certificate, or supervise it?","options":["neither","supervision","unintentional omission"],"answer":"unintentional omission","strata":{"frame":"active-verb","sense":"miss"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-06","english":"The reviewers unintentionally failed to include the accessibility exception in their summary.","ainglish":"The reviewers overslipped the accessibility exception in their summary.","question":"What happened to the exception: it was accidentally omitted, or it was supervised?","options":["unintentional omission","neither","supervision"],"answer":"unintentional omission","strata":{"frame":"active-verb","sense":"miss"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-07","english":"The duplicate account was unintentionally missed by both validation passes.","ainglish":"The duplicate account was overslipped by both validation passes.","question":"Was the account monitored successfully, or accidentally not noticed?","options":["supervision","unintentional omission","neither"],"answer":"unintentional omission","strata":{"frame":"passive-verb","sense":"miss"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-08","english":"A tiny unintentional omission left the timezone conversion out of the runbook.","ainglish":"A tiny overslip left the timezone conversion out of the runbook.","question":"Does the noun name governance of the runbook or a missed detail?","options":["neither","supervision","unintentional omission"],"answer":"unintentional omission","strata":{"frame":"cold-noun","sense":"miss"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-09","english":"Independent supervision of the bridge inspection remains with the safety office.","ainglish":"Independent oversight of the bridge inspection remains with the safety office.","question":"Does the sentence assign supervision or report an accidental omission?","options":["unintentional omission","neither","supervision"],"answer":"supervision","strata":{"frame":"genitive-noun","sense":"supervision"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-10","english":"The board provides continuing supervision while the remediation plan is executed.","ainglish":"The board provides continuing oversight while the remediation plan is executed.","question":"What does the board provide: monitoring authority or an unintentional miss?","options":["supervision","unintentional omission","neither"],"answer":"supervision","strata":{"frame":"predicate-noun","sense":"supervision"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-11","english":"External supervision is mandatory for every release of the diagnostic model.","ainglish":"External oversight is mandatory for every release of the diagnostic model.","question":"Is an external party required to monitor releases, or accidentally omit them?","options":["neither","supervision","unintentional omission"],"answer":"supervision","strata":{"frame":"compound-noun","sense":"supervision"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-12","english":"The regulator strengthened its supervision after the reporting breach.","ainglish":"The regulator strengthened its oversight after the reporting breach.","question":"What was strengthened: the regulator\u0027s monitoring, or an accidental omission?","options":["unintentional omission","neither","supervision"],"answer":"supervision","strata":{"frame":"possessive-noun","sense":"supervision"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-13","english":"Clinical supervision of the trial includes weekly review of adverse events.","ainglish":"Clinical oversight of the trial includes weekly review of adverse events.","question":"Does the phrase describe active monitoring or an unnoticed missing item?","options":["supervision","unintentional omission","neither"],"answer":"supervision","strata":{"frame":"genitive-noun","sense":"supervision"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-14","english":"Budget supervision is shared by the treasury team and the elected committee.","ainglish":"Budget oversight is shared by the treasury team and the elected committee.","question":"Are the two groups sharing governance or sharing an accidental mistake?","options":["neither","supervision","unintentional omission"],"answer":"supervision","strata":{"frame":"compound-noun","sense":"supervision"}},{"id":"r9-overslip-15","english":"Human supervision remains available whenever the autonomous loader encounters an exception.","ainglish":"Human oversight remains available whenever the autonomous loader encounters an exceptio